title: "CodeObf-PI v1.0: measuring and repairing the encoding shortcut in lightweight prompt-injection detectors for code"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Peiyuan"
    affiliation: "Nanjing University of Information Science and Technology"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-7982-9597"
year: 2026
version: "1.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - encoded prompts
  - LLM guardrails
  - code-reading agents
  - de-confounding
  - dataset
abstract: >-
  Controlled dataset and reference implementation for auditing whether lightweight
  prompt-injection detectors respond to malicious intent or merely to the presence of
  an encoding. Nine encodings are crossed with two carriers, and each malicious prompt
  is paired with a benign prompt built from the same prefix base. The package contains
  data-construction, baseline, fine-tuning, evaluation and audit scripts, the frozen
  train/validation splits, the result tables and the figures. The sealed test split and
  the LoRA adapters are not included.
